            <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Do I need to prime before painting a deck?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">Bare wood always benefits from a quality exterior primer. Tannin-rich woods (cedar, redwood) need a stain-blocking primer. Previously painted decks in good condition may skip primer for similar-color repaints. Resurfacers are typically self-priming. When in doubt, prime.</p>
